# engine.manifest — the whitelist of paths that are "engine": pure tooling, safe to copy in
# either direction between two JobHuntKit-shaped checkouts, and guaranteed (by construction, not
# by discipline) to never carry personal data.
#
# Read by two things:
#   scripts/sync.sh          — pull copies these paths FROM a canonical repo INTO your root;
#                               push copies them FROM your root INTO a canonical repo. Nothing
#                               outside this list is ever touched in either direction.
#   scripts/audit_public.py  — the leak gate that runs before every push. It also refuses to run
#                               at all if this file itself ever lists one of the forbidden
#                               content prefixes (profile/, master/, applications/, produced/,
#                               workspace/, config.json) — belt and suspenders.
#
# One path per line, relative to the repo root. A trailing "/" means "this whole directory tree";
# without one it means "exactly this file". Blank lines and lines starting with "#" are ignored.
# A path that doesn't exist yet (a future milestone's file) is skipped quietly, not an error —
# so this file can forward-declare paths before they're built.

engine/
scripts/
templates/
agents/
docs/
examples/
tests/
.claude/
.cursor/
.github/
demo.sh
README.md
LICENSE
NOTICE
CONTRIBUTING.md
AGENTS.md
config.example.json
requirements-dev.txt
engine.manifest
.private-terms.example
.gitignore
